Copper oxychloride (dicopper chloride trihydroxide) is classified in HTSUS 2827.39 (chlorides, other), with 2827.39.60 covering "Other chlorides: Of copper" and 2827.41 covering chloride oxides and chloride hydroxides of copper. Subheading 2827.41.00 is "Chloride oxides and chloride hydroxides: of copper". Dicopper chloride trihydroxide is a chloride hydroxide of copper, so it goes in 2827.41. Its statistical suffix is 2827.41.0000.

The CBP ruling on this product (feed-grade tribasic copper chloride) also classified it in 2827.41.0000. The fact that it is sold for animal feed does not change this, because it is a separate chemically defined compound and is not a prepared feed under 2309.

{"hts_code": "2827.41.0000", "reason": "Tribasic copper chloride, Cu2(OH)3Cl, is a chemically defined chloride hydroxide of copper, classified in HTSUS subheading 2827.41 (chloride oxides and chloride hydroxides of copper)."}
